        "original_id": "ca8a07e9-e244-5d1b-9223-1210fe8535b0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Edith Bouvier Beale, Edith Ewing Bouvier, Drew Barrymore, Jessica Lange, Jeanne Tripplehorn, Jacqueline Kennedy, Ken Howard, Phelan Beale, Michael Sucsy\n- Works: Grey Gardens, Flight of the Conchords, The New Cup\n- Organizations: HBO\n- Roles: attorney, sportsman\n\nFacts:\n- Phelan Beale was born on May 23, 1881 and died on June 12, 1956.\n- Phelan Beale was an American attorney and sportsman in New York City.\n- Phelan Beale was married to Edith Ewing Bouvier, who was an aunt of Jacqueline Kennedy Onassis.\n- Grey Gardens is an HBO film about the lives of Edith Bouvier Beale and her mother Edith Ewing Bouvier.\n- Drew Barrymore played Little Edie, and Jessica Lange played Big Edie, in Grey Gardens.\n- Jeanne Tripplehorn co-starred in Grey Gardens as Jacqueline Kennedy, who was Little Edie's cousin.\n- Ken Howard co-starred in Grey Gardens as Phelan Beale, who was Little Edie's father.\n- Michael Sucsy is best known for creating the HBO film Grey Gardens.\n- The New Cup is the second episode of the second season of the HBO comedy series Flight of the Conchords.\n- The New Cup is the fourteenth episode overall of Flight of the Conchords.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
